finding: DrawRegistry retains deleted values in the base Registry Map but does not override Registry[Symbol.iterator](), which returns that Map's values directly rather than dispatching to the overridden values(). Thus for-of, spread and Array.from(Draws) expose removed mesh draws and preserve first insertion order rather than live re-registration order, while has/get/size/values/forEach hide them. Reproduced in a scratch clone by adding expect([...world.resource(Draws)].some(draw => draw.mesh === handle)).toBe(false) immediately after removal in membership.node.ts: expected false, received true, although bounds and has() assertions pass. This fails stage 3's storage reuse for every consumer and the explicit registry-iteration stale-state requirement. Override Symbol.iterator to use live iteration and cover removal/re-registration order across all iteration APIs. Required turnover oracle, Rendering iteration plus render allocation oracle (322 pass), membership, voxel terrain and lint otherwise passed; restored Float32Array bounds and draw-image allocations independently fail the turnover oracle with 12000 B per window at their respective owners.
